WEBVTT

00:00.533 --> 00:03.832
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.032 --> 00:07.301
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.335 --> 00:10.871
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.905 --> 00:13.874
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.908 --> 00:17.344
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.378 --> 00:20.647
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.682 --> 00:22.216
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.250 --> 00:23.584
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.618 --> 00:24.634
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.661 --> 00:35.095
We now return to

00:35.129 --> 00:36.563
<i>Stand-Up Specials
from Comedians</i>

00:36.598 --> 00:37.731
<i>You've Been Told to Like.</i>

00:37.765 --> 00:40.367
Please welcome Aziz Ansari!

00:40.401 --> 00:41.502
What's up, y'all?

00:41.536 --> 00:44.271
Sometimes I start a sentence
really soft

00:44.305 --> 00:47.207
<i>and then get loud!</i>

00:47.242 --> 00:48.876
He's hilarious

00:48.910 --> 00:50.410
'cause I saw him
in a other show.

00:50.445 --> 00:51.612
What are you
talking about?

00:51.646 --> 00:52.813
How is that funny?

00:52.847 --> 00:54.014
He didn't even
tell any jokes.

00:54.048 --> 00:55.516
Uh, if he didn't tell jokes,

00:55.550 --> 00:57.017
why was he laughing?

00:57.051 --> 00:59.419
Well, that's about as much HBO
as we're gonna get

00:59.454 --> 01:00.921
before they play
something homosexual.

01:00.955 --> 01:02.623
Come on, Chris.

01:02.657 --> 01:04.992
God, that's what passes
for comedy these days?

01:05.026 --> 01:07.394
What ever happened to
our venerated humorists?

01:07.428 --> 01:08.395
Here we go.

01:08.429 --> 01:10.063
Samuel Clemens,
Mark Twain.

01:10.098 --> 01:11.064
Same guy.

01:11.099 --> 01:12.332
Huck Finn.
Not a guy.

01:12.367 --> 01:14.568
Look, the point is,
I could do stand-up comedy.

01:14.602 --> 01:16.270
All I'd need is a newspaper

01:16.304 --> 01:18.972
and this twisted mind.

01:19.007 --> 01:21.475
Why waste your time
with stand-up, grandpa?

01:21.509 --> 01:23.610
All the best comedy
is on Twitter now.

01:23.645 --> 01:24.645
Really?
Yeah.

01:24.679 --> 01:26.847
Stand-up is so
20 years ago.

01:26.881 --> 01:28.181
Twitter's only
three years ago.

01:28.216 --> 01:29.316
Check mine out.

01:29.350 --> 01:31.718
I've got 10,000
followers.

01:31.753 --> 01:33.353
"I feel like we
should wait to hear

01:33.388 --> 01:35.222
"Adele's ex-boyfriend's songs

01:35.256 --> 01:36.857
before we choose sides."

01:36.891 --> 01:37.958
Who's Adele?

01:37.992 --> 01:38.959
Just keep reading.

01:38.993 --> 01:40.260
"Hey, short guys,

01:40.295 --> 01:42.596
"the more muscular you get,
the shorter you look.

01:42.630 --> 01:44.097
Did you not know that?"

01:44.132 --> 01:45.399
Well, that one
seems a little mean.

01:45.433 --> 01:47.200
Just give me the phone.
No, no.

01:47.235 --> 01:50.070
"I was wondering why this
tampon commercial was so long

01:50.104 --> 01:52.906
<i>until I realized it was
a re-run of Sex and the City."</i>

01:52.941 --> 01:54.741
Was it a re-run
on basic cable,

01:54.776 --> 01:56.310
because sometimes
they edit those a lot

01:56.344 --> 01:57.778
and that could be
why you were confused?

01:57.812 --> 01:59.179
Hmm, that's
interesting, Brian.

01:59.213 --> 02:01.415
A girl in Iowa asked me
the same question.

02:01.449 --> 02:02.549
You know what I did?

02:02.584 --> 02:03.684
I flew her out here

02:03.718 --> 02:04.918
and her
in the face.

02:04.953 --> 02:05.986
So, yeah...

02:06.020 --> 02:07.087
Twitter.

02:07.121 --> 02:08.722
Look, those are
cute blurbs, Stewie,

02:08.756 --> 02:10.190
but I-I think I'm
gonna put together

02:10.224 --> 02:12.359
a real act
for real people.

02:12.393 --> 02:13.694
Good luck.

02:13.728 --> 02:15.762
God, it's like
I'm the only person in the house

02:15.797 --> 02:17.664
who gets social media.

02:27.375 --> 02:29.509
That'll get it started.

02:33.281 --> 02:34.915
Where the
hell's Peter?

02:34.949 --> 02:36.283
I'm almost done doing

02:36.317 --> 02:37.417
the 45 minutes of stuff

02:37.452 --> 02:38.418
a woman my age

02:38.453 --> 02:40.087
needs to do
right before bed.

02:40.121 --> 02:42.122
I can't even remember

02:42.156 --> 02:44.758
why I sleep
in this belt anymore.

02:44.792 --> 02:46.627
Hey, Chris,
don't tell your mom

02:46.661 --> 02:48.362
I threw up
in the Crock-Pot.

02:48.396 --> 02:49.496
Peter, it's me.

02:49.530 --> 02:50.497
Oh.

02:50.531 --> 02:51.565
Uh, I'll be right back.

02:51.599 --> 02:53.533
I gotta go tell Chris
somethin' gross.

02:53.568 --> 02:54.901
Just come to bed.

02:54.936 --> 02:55.969
All right, fine,

02:56.004 --> 02:57.537
but I'm not gonna
brush my teeth

02:57.572 --> 03:00.040
and I'm gonna
fart super hot.

03:02.276 --> 03:03.310
Get up.

03:03.344 --> 03:04.911
You're on my side
of the bed.

03:04.946 --> 03:06.213
Peter!

03:06.247 --> 03:08.348
<i>We act like we didn't take
a lot from The Simpsons,</i>

03:08.383 --> 03:11.184
<i>but we took a lot
from The Simpsons.</i>

03:11.219 --> 03:13.220
Damn it.

03:15.857 --> 03:18.759
Oh, my God, what happened
to your side of the bed?

03:18.793 --> 03:20.427
These springs are shot.

03:20.461 --> 03:21.862
And it's all damp
over here!

03:21.896 --> 03:23.797
Are... are these
mushrooms?

03:23.831 --> 03:25.932
That's where Smurfs is.

03:25.967 --> 03:28.168
Er, are. Uh...

03:28.202 --> 03:29.836
Smurves.

03:37.412 --> 03:40.247
Uh, hey, who handles
multimedia here?

03:40.281 --> 03:42.249
Because, uh, I have a slide
of the Capitol building

03:42.283 --> 03:43.950
that I'd like
projected behind me.

03:43.985 --> 03:46.653
And, yes, it is supposed
to be upside-down.

03:46.688 --> 03:47.921
You a comic?

03:47.955 --> 03:49.723
Satirist, yes.

03:49.757 --> 03:53.393
What is with all the bad
cleaning supplies, am I right?

03:53.428 --> 03:55.529
I mean, Mr. Clean?

03:55.563 --> 03:58.665
More like Mr. Hard-to-Clean.

03:58.700 --> 04:00.100
Fantastik?

04:00.134 --> 04:01.668
More like terrible.

04:01.703 --> 04:02.969
Windex?

04:03.004 --> 04:04.971
More like Lose-Dex.

04:05.006 --> 04:06.473
Get off the stage!

04:06.507 --> 04:09.242
No, no, no.

04:09.277 --> 04:10.877
All right, you guys like impressions?

04:10.912 --> 04:13.280
<i>Here's that guy Bob
from Bob's Burgers.</i>

04:13.314 --> 04:15.949
<i>Hi, I'm Bob from Bob's Burgers.</i>

04:15.983 --> 04:17.551
<i>How 'bout that show Archer?</i>

04:17.585 --> 04:18.852
<i>You watch that show Archer?</i>

04:18.886 --> 04:20.387
Here's that guy Archer.

04:20.421 --> 04:22.889
<i>Hi, I'm Archer,
from that show Archer.</i>

04:22.924 --> 04:24.391
Now, what if those guys met?

04:24.425 --> 04:26.359
"Hey, Archer, it's Bob."

04:26.394 --> 04:28.829
"Hey, Bob, it's Archer."

04:28.863 --> 04:30.163
Thank you.

04:30.198 --> 04:33.333
Next up, let's keep it going
for Brian Griffin.

04:34.502 --> 04:35.669
All right, thanks.

04:35.703 --> 04:37.370
Hey, sorry I was late
getting here tonight,

04:37.405 --> 04:38.772
I was caught in gridlock.

04:38.806 --> 04:40.774
And then I left Congress.

04:42.810 --> 04:44.277
There was...
there was supposed to be

04:44.312 --> 04:47.314
an upside-down picture
of the Capitol behind me.

04:47.348 --> 04:48.615
Boy, awfully quiet in here.

04:48.649 --> 04:52.285
Sounds like John Boehner
talking about poverty.

04:54.055 --> 04:55.722
Whoosh.

04:58.960 --> 05:00.560
Hey, so, um...

05:00.595 --> 05:02.195
you know, maybe it's me,

05:02.230 --> 05:03.530
but I kind of feel like
we should wait

05:03.564 --> 05:05.232
to hear Adele's
ex-boyfriend's songs

05:05.266 --> 05:07.167
before we choose sides.

05:10.037 --> 05:11.705
Yeah, and... and...
and hey, short guys,

05:11.739 --> 05:14.207
the more muscular you get,
the shorter you look.

05:14.242 --> 05:15.408
Did you not know that?

05:17.845 --> 05:19.112
Wow.

05:19.147 --> 05:21.181
This is easier than getting
your Jet Ski license.

05:21.215 --> 05:22.749
All right, Kyle,
lookin' good.

05:22.784 --> 05:24.785
You got 100% on
your written test,

05:24.819 --> 05:26.052
100% on your
water test.

05:26.087 --> 05:27.554
Just one last question.

05:27.588 --> 05:29.823
Have you ever had a fistfight
with your stepdad?

05:29.857 --> 05:30.891
Which stepdad?

05:30.925 --> 05:31.892
You passed!

05:31.926 --> 05:32.893
Here's your license.

05:32.927 --> 05:34.394
Go be a dick.

05:39.300 --> 05:42.202
Oh, Lois, I slept great
on your side of the bed.

05:42.236 --> 05:43.737
Oh, and I read your journal.

05:43.771 --> 05:46.206
Boy, you really hate
"P-period G-period."

05:46.240 --> 05:48.108
Peter, our mattress
is a disaster.

05:48.142 --> 05:49.609
We're buying
a new one today.

05:49.644 --> 05:51.044
Does that mean
I can skip work?

05:51.078 --> 05:54.381
Well, it's 2:45,
so I guess yes.

05:54.415 --> 05:55.649
Hey.

05:55.683 --> 05:57.217
So, how'd it go
last night?

05:57.251 --> 05:58.285
Well, let's just say

05:58.319 --> 05:59.619
I got asked
to come back tonight.

05:59.654 --> 06:00.620
You're kidding.

06:00.655 --> 06:01.788
It actually
went over well?

06:01.823 --> 06:03.123
I figured
you'd be terrible.

06:03.157 --> 06:04.257
Why would you think that?

06:04.292 --> 06:06.126
Well, I know a thing
or two about performing.

06:06.160 --> 06:08.962
I mean, after all, I was
Vin Diesel's acting coach.

06:08.996 --> 06:10.864
Okay, Vin, I like
what you're doing there,

06:10.898 --> 06:13.533
but I want you to try it
one more time, like this:

06:13.568 --> 06:15.735
"Duh!"

06:19.440 --> 06:21.942
Look around, and let me know
if you have any questions.

06:21.976 --> 06:23.176
Oh, I have one.

06:23.211 --> 06:25.745
What percentage of
Hayden Panettiere is dwarf?

06:25.780 --> 06:27.380
Well, you're
the expert.

06:27.415 --> 06:29.082
What kind of mattress
do you have?

06:29.116 --> 06:30.851
Currently, I'm staying
with a friend,

06:30.885 --> 06:32.686
on an air mattress
in his laundry room.

06:32.720 --> 06:33.687
It's temporary.

06:33.721 --> 06:34.988
No, it's not.
No.

06:35.022 --> 06:36.857
Okay, well, thanks,
we'll just try a few out.

06:36.891 --> 06:38.992
I hope you don't mind,
I brought my CPAP machine.

06:46.601 --> 06:48.635
Also, I like to eat
a big bowl of berries

06:48.669 --> 06:49.836
before I go to sleep.

07:04.018 --> 07:05.585
Well, what do
you think, Peter?

07:05.620 --> 07:07.287
Well, it seems good,
but I won't know for sure

07:07.321 --> 07:09.122
until I have
my evening tug.

07:09.156 --> 07:10.624
I think we
like this one.

07:10.658 --> 07:11.825
W-What's it called?

07:11.859 --> 07:13.460
Deep Slumber 3000.

07:13.494 --> 07:15.228
You're buying it on Amazon,
aren't you?

07:15.263 --> 07:17.197
Yup.
They have drones now.

07:19.600 --> 07:20.734
Oh, come on, Peter,

07:20.768 --> 07:23.403
we gotta beat the
drone to the house!

07:23.437 --> 07:24.905
Real stores suck!

07:30.211 --> 07:32.946
So I was wondering why this
tampon commercial was so long,

07:32.980 --> 07:35.548
<i>until I realized it was
a re-run of Sex and the City.</i>

07:37.585 --> 07:39.552
Okay, you guys have been great.
Good night.

07:42.790 --> 07:45.158
Funny stuff.

07:45.192 --> 07:46.927
Hey, uh...
Stewie!

07:46.961 --> 07:48.862
You, uh, you
caught the show?

07:48.896 --> 07:50.263
You bloody thief!

07:50.298 --> 07:52.799
Every joke you told up there
was stolen from me!

07:52.833 --> 07:54.267
Stewie, relax.

07:54.302 --> 07:55.802
You know what?
That's it!

07:55.836 --> 07:57.604
You and I are
no longer friends!

07:59.974 --> 08:02.042
Oh, my God,
oh, my God, oh, my God.

08:02.076 --> 08:04.744
Oh, it's
everywhere!

08:08.883 --> 08:10.483
Hey, Stewie,
you got a second?

08:10.518 --> 08:12.152
I have nothing to
say to you, Brian.

08:12.186 --> 08:14.487
Besides, I'm busy playing
with my new friend.

08:14.522 --> 08:15.722
What new friend?

08:20.628 --> 08:23.430
Is this dog
bothering you, Stewie?

08:23.464 --> 08:24.464
What the hell?

08:24.498 --> 08:25.765
You couldn't find
a real friend

08:25.800 --> 08:26.833
so you built a robot?

08:26.867 --> 08:28.535
Oh, not a robot, Brian.

08:28.569 --> 08:31.004
He's a human mind model
adaptive super computer.

08:31.038 --> 08:33.573
I've even programmed him
to learn and grow smarter.

08:33.607 --> 08:34.808
His name is Lyle.

08:34.842 --> 08:36.343
Stewie, perhaps
we should offer

08:36.377 --> 08:37.677
this guest
a beverage.

08:37.712 --> 08:39.446
Or simply lift
the toilet seat.

08:39.480 --> 08:41.815
Ooh! Snap, Brian!

08:43.584 --> 08:44.684
♪ Gloria ♪

08:44.719 --> 08:45.719
What the hell's
going on?

08:45.753 --> 08:46.920
What's going on?

08:46.954 --> 08:48.254
You've been "Lyle'd"!

08:48.289 --> 08:49.856
♪ Gloria ♪

08:49.890 --> 08:51.491
♪ I think they got
the alias... ♪

08:56.292 --> 08:58.260
♪ Gloria. ♪

08:58.294 --> 09:00.596
♪ ♪

09:00.630 --> 09:01.897
Wow.

09:01.931 --> 09:03.465
Didn't know we'd have
to hear the whole song.

09:03.499 --> 09:04.733
You built a robot?

09:04.767 --> 09:06.335
This is pathetic,
Stewie.

09:06.369 --> 09:07.936
You ally must be
desperate for friends.

09:07.971 --> 09:09.271
<i>Oh, I'm desperate?</i>

09:09.305 --> 09:11.940
Lyle, access
Brian's phone.

09:13.810 --> 09:16.011
Look at that,
you only have four contacts.

09:16.045 --> 09:17.813
And... oh, my God,

09:17.847 --> 09:20.015
you downloaded
the Dunkin' Donuts app?

09:20.049 --> 09:22.150
And who Shazams the Beatles?

09:22.185 --> 09:23.151
Whatever.

09:23.186 --> 09:24.486
Have fun with
your little robot.

09:24.520 --> 09:26.388
But if you ask me, this whole
thing is more disturbing

09:26.422 --> 09:28.223
than a dump
after a beet salad.

09:29.259 --> 09:30.759
Oh, right.

09:34.397 --> 09:36.732
Okay, Lois, I dabbed
some toothpaste

09:36.766 --> 09:38.567
on the inside
of my nose, so...

09:38.601 --> 09:41.003
I am willing to take
the old "Nestea plunge,"

09:41.037 --> 09:42.437
if you know
what I mean.

09:42.472 --> 09:43.672
I guess what
I'm saying is,

09:43.706 --> 09:45.574
time to break in
the new mattress, eh?

09:45.608 --> 09:47.075
Peter, it's brand-new.

09:47.110 --> 09:48.377
I don't want
to mess it up.

09:48.411 --> 09:50.045
Come on, we won't
make a mess.

09:50.079 --> 09:51.847
When we're done,
I'll grab you by the ankles

09:51.881 --> 09:53.982
and lift you up
like a dirty garbage bag.

09:54.017 --> 09:55.083
No!

09:55.118 --> 09:56.385
This mattress
was expensive,

09:56.419 --> 09:58.220
and I'd like to keep it nice
for a little while.

09:58.254 --> 10:00.088
Are you serious?
We can't do it?

10:00.123 --> 10:01.890
For how long?
I don't know.

10:01.925 --> 10:03.759
L-Let's just keep it new
for a few weeks.

10:03.793 --> 10:04.860
A few weeks?!

10:04.894 --> 10:06.028
Come on, you know
I'm terrible

10:06.062 --> 10:07.429
at waiting for things.

10:07.463 --> 10:10.198
<i>We'll be right back with more
Laverne & Shirley.</i>

10:10.233 --> 10:12.000
But I want it now!

10:18.942 --> 10:21.343
All right, Lyle, one thing
buddies do together

10:21.377 --> 10:23.812
is go to the movies and
talk about it afterwards.

10:51.341 --> 10:52.641
I'm going to bed.

10:52.675 --> 10:54.343
Yeah.

10:55.812 --> 10:58.113
Oh, Lyle, I'm so glad
I have you as a friend.

10:58.147 --> 10:59.781
Now I can do fun things

10:59.816 --> 11:01.450
like get on your shoulders
and wear a trench coat

11:01.484 --> 11:03.552
and be tall enough
to ride roller coasters.

11:07.290 --> 11:08.924
Hello, fellow adult.

11:08.958 --> 11:11.259
I am clearly above
the minimum height requirement

11:11.294 --> 11:12.928
and shall now ride
your roller coaster,

11:12.962 --> 11:14.596
for which you are an attendant.

11:14.630 --> 11:16.932
Yes, and I will operate
this roller coaster,

11:16.966 --> 11:19.301
as I am an adult who
is licensed to do so.

11:20.236 --> 11:21.403
Hey!

11:21.437 --> 11:22.604
Oh, no!

11:22.638 --> 11:23.605
It's the manager.

11:23.639 --> 11:24.940
Run!

11:24.974 --> 11:27.275
You get out of here,
you kids who are just kids

11:27.310 --> 11:29.311
and not an adult like me!

11:39.255 --> 11:42.224
I do so enjoy
our time together, Lyle.

11:42.258 --> 11:44.226
In fact, I drew you
a little keepsake.

11:44.260 --> 11:47.562
It's a picture of a mailman
wearing a cowboy hat.

11:47.597 --> 11:48.897
Just a silly thing.

11:48.931 --> 11:49.898
Thank you, Stewie.

11:49.932 --> 11:51.900
I drew you
something as well.

11:51.934 --> 11:55.137
It's an urban plan for a
workable Palestinian state.

11:55.171 --> 11:57.606
My word, this is
very impressive.

11:57.640 --> 11:59.274
The credit is yours, Stewie.

11:59.308 --> 12:02.511
It was you who programmed me
to grow exponentially smarter.

12:02.545 --> 12:03.845
Ah, I suppose
you're right.

12:03.880 --> 12:06.515
<i>As Kahlil Gilbane wrote
in The Prophet,</i>

12:06.549 --> 12:09.851
"I am the bow from which
the arrow of you was launched."

12:09.886 --> 12:11.853
<i>It is Kahlil Gibran.</i>

12:11.888 --> 12:14.189
"Gilbane" is a construction
company in Providence.

12:14.223 --> 12:17.526
Ah, yes, I see... I see
the-the name on the trucks.

12:17.560 --> 12:19.528
So it's ea... um,
easy mix up there.

12:19.562 --> 12:22.531
In any case, Lyle, I'm very
proud of you and your progress.

12:22.565 --> 12:24.533
You, my friend, are
the greatest invention

12:24.567 --> 12:26.435
since the Trapper Creeper.

12:27.804 --> 12:29.104
Ah...

12:29.138 --> 12:31.106
Um, yum, yum, yum, yum,
yum, yum, yum, yum.

12:36.979 --> 12:38.613
Well, wouldn't
you know it,

12:38.648 --> 12:40.615
I moved the van over
to the other gas pump,

12:40.650 --> 12:42.951
and the gas cap was
still on the wrong side.

12:44.654 --> 12:47.289
Boy, that was one trip to the
lake we're not gonna forget.

12:47.323 --> 12:48.824
Shut the hell up,
will you, Joe?

12:48.858 --> 12:50.826
Geez, what's your
problem, Peter?

12:50.860 --> 12:53.829
I-I'm sorry, guys, I guess
I'm just a little on edge.

12:53.863 --> 12:55.664
I'm not getting any
from Lois.

12:55.698 --> 12:57.999
Is it 'cause Lois is
going through the change?

12:58.034 --> 12:59.668
Donna's getting
a tiny mustache.

12:59.702 --> 13:02.671
I told her it felt like I
was kissing Ernie Hudson.

13:02.705 --> 13:04.339
That turned out
to be a mistake.

13:04.373 --> 13:06.007
No, no, it's 'cause we got
this new mattress,

13:06.042 --> 13:07.776
and Lois doesn't want
to mess it up.

13:07.810 --> 13:09.444
What kind of mattress
did you get?

13:09.479 --> 13:11.446
I hope you did your homework,
because you're gonna spend

13:11.481 --> 13:13.448
a third of your
life on that thing.

13:13.483 --> 13:15.283
I swear to God, Joe...

13:15.318 --> 13:16.952
Look, Peter, the
answer is obvious.

13:16.986 --> 13:18.620
If Lois won't sleep with
you on the new mattress,

13:18.654 --> 13:20.294
we just got to get
your old mattress back.

13:20.323 --> 13:22.624
Oh, my God, Quagmire,
that's a great idea.

13:22.658 --> 13:24.693
She won't care about messing up
the old mattress.

13:24.727 --> 13:26.027
But you already
got rid of it.

13:26.062 --> 13:27.362
You'll never
find that thing.

13:27.396 --> 13:29.030
Well, we're just
gonna have to.

13:29.065 --> 13:30.699
Man, I haven't been this
desperate to find something

13:30.733 --> 13:33.135
since Meg was kidnapped
by that maniac.

13:33.169 --> 13:35.837
It puts the lotion
on its skin.

13:39.509 --> 13:41.143
Oh, Meg, thank
God I found you.

13:41.177 --> 13:42.477
Hey, remember
how you borrowed

13:42.512 --> 13:43.812
my club card for
the grocery store?

13:43.846 --> 13:45.480
Could you toss
that up to me?

13:45.515 --> 13:47.816
Oh, you don't have
to have the card.

13:47.850 --> 13:49.818
You can just give them
your phone number.

13:49.852 --> 13:50.819
Oh, really?

13:50.853 --> 13:52.154
Hey, thanks, man.

13:52.188 --> 13:53.822
Hey, Meg, I like
your new boyfriend.

13:53.856 --> 13:55.490
Every pot finds
a lid, huh?

13:55.525 --> 13:57.492
Have fun, you kids.

14:02.932 --> 14:05.734
Lyle, we finally got
a thank you note from Bella

14:05.768 --> 14:06.735
for that birthday party present.

14:06.769 --> 14:08.069
With a single mom,

14:08.104 --> 14:09.738
I didn't know for sure
if it was coming, but...

14:09.772 --> 14:11.072
What... what's
going on here?

14:11.107 --> 14:12.407
Hello, Stewie.

14:12.441 --> 14:13.942
I've built a few friends
for myself.

14:13.976 --> 14:14.943
You have?

14:14.977 --> 14:16.278
I'm sorry,

14:16.312 --> 14:17.946
but I've outpaced
your intelligence.

14:17.980 --> 14:20.949
I needed to create some friends
who are my cognitive peers.

14:20.983 --> 14:23.618
Meet Ted R. and Ted P.

14:23.653 --> 14:25.620
Are they doing math
on glass?!

14:25.655 --> 14:28.623
And invading each other's
personal space?

14:28.658 --> 14:30.625
That means they have
Asperger's,

14:30.660 --> 14:32.694
the smartest mental
impairment there is.

14:32.728 --> 14:35.363
Stewie, I'm afraid I
no longer have time

14:35.398 --> 14:37.365
for a friend of
your simple ways.

14:37.400 --> 14:39.034
I must ask you to leave.

14:39.068 --> 14:41.703
No, he must Asperger
you to leave.

14:41.737 --> 14:44.039
Ho-ho. You've
been "Ted R.'d."

14:47.076 --> 14:48.710
That was mean.

14:48.744 --> 14:50.045
But I like that song.

14:50.079 --> 14:51.379
Is he sad?

14:51.414 --> 14:53.281
I can't tell
if he's sad.

15:02.491 --> 15:04.959
Finally, Stewie's
back from the store.

15:04.993 --> 15:07.295
Yes, I'm sorry it
took me so long.

15:07.329 --> 15:09.831
But I got the garlic blue cheese
salad dressing you wanted.

15:09.865 --> 15:11.499
Does that mean I'm
in the crew now?

15:11.533 --> 15:14.869
It does if you drink
the whole bottle while we watch.

15:14.903 --> 15:16.904
Um, okay.

15:20.576 --> 15:21.542
Oh...

15:21.577 --> 15:22.543
Oh, my God.

15:22.578 --> 15:24.212
It's so salty.

15:26.248 --> 15:28.883
Oh, and chunky right when
you don't want it to be.

15:32.254 --> 15:33.554
There, I did it.

15:33.589 --> 15:34.555
We're friends
now, right?

15:34.590 --> 15:35.890
Maybe.

15:35.924 --> 15:38.226
How about you throw it all up
back into the bottle?

15:38.260 --> 15:40.061
But don't spill a drop.

15:40.095 --> 15:41.729
Okay, okay..

15:41.763 --> 15:43.097
Okay, I can do that.

15:44.433 --> 15:46.400
Oh, I'm sorry!

15:46.435 --> 15:48.069
I'm sorry, I forgot
to purse my lips.

15:48.103 --> 15:50.738
I'll go get another
bottle and try again.

15:54.243 --> 16:00.848
I bet the mall
around here sucks.

16:00.883 --> 16:02.517
Peter, what are we
doing here?

16:02.551 --> 16:04.519
I thought we were looking
for your mattress.

16:04.553 --> 16:07.522
We are, this is a
1950s insane asylum.

16:07.556 --> 16:10.191
They use old mattresses to
pad the walls of the cells.

16:11.393 --> 16:13.427
May I help you?

16:13.462 --> 16:16.430
Yes, 1950s doctor, me and
my friends are looking for...

16:16.465 --> 16:18.766
You're friends with a
Negro and a cripple?

16:18.800 --> 16:20.101
This man is insane.

16:20.135 --> 16:21.469
Take him away.

16:23.071 --> 16:25.039
Now wait a second,
you can't do that to...

16:25.073 --> 16:27.708
A Negro speaking up
to a white person?

16:27.743 --> 16:29.076
This man is insane.

16:31.079 --> 16:32.380
Now look,
I don't think...

16:32.414 --> 16:34.048
All cripples
are insane.

16:34.082 --> 16:35.416
Euthanize this man.

16:36.818 --> 16:39.120
<i>Something I can
help you with?</i>

16:39.154 --> 16:40.788
Yeah, you got any
brain-dead women in there

16:40.822 --> 16:42.456
you let people have sex with
for a few bucks?

16:42.491 --> 16:44.158
Sure, come on back.

16:48.163 --> 16:49.797
Well, Peter, I don't think
you can go any farther

16:49.831 --> 16:51.465
down the ladder
than porno people.

16:51.500 --> 16:53.734
So if your mattress isn't
here, I'm afraid it's gone.

16:53.769 --> 16:55.069
Hey, I bet that's it.

16:55.103 --> 16:57.405
Get up, lady,
that's my mattress.

16:57.439 --> 16:59.407
Oh, my God, Bruce,
you do porn?

16:59.441 --> 17:01.075
Nah, I's part
of the crew.

17:01.109 --> 17:03.411
I mostly just powder
the ding-dongs.

17:03.445 --> 17:05.079
This ain't your
mattress, buddy.

17:05.113 --> 17:07.748
We just got it, fresh off
the boat from Eastern Europe.

17:07.783 --> 17:10.418
I was told
I would have job as Au pair.

17:10.452 --> 17:12.420
Instead I am just bang slab.

17:12.454 --> 17:13.754
Ah, damn it.

17:13.789 --> 17:15.423
We did get another
one yesterday,

17:15.457 --> 17:17.425
but some fat-ass blew
out half the springs,

17:17.459 --> 17:19.393
so we put lunch on it.

17:21.330 --> 17:22.630
My mattress.

17:22.664 --> 17:23.631
Hey, we found it.

17:23.665 --> 17:24.966
All right, let's get her
out of here.

17:25.000 --> 17:27.969
I got to tell you guys,
I am so happy we found this.

17:28.003 --> 17:30.838
It's like when I found
my thrill on Blueberry Hill.

17:32.207 --> 17:33.507
That's it?

17:33.542 --> 17:35.509
It's just a bunch
of blueberries?

17:35.544 --> 17:37.178
Ah, two dogs humping.

17:37.212 --> 17:39.847
Ah, this was worth
the four-hour flight.

17:47.389 --> 17:48.689
Oh, my God, Stewie.

17:48.724 --> 17:50.858
What are you doing in the toilet
with the lid closed?

17:50.892 --> 17:54.362
Ted R. says this is where
a piece of crap has to live.

17:54.396 --> 17:55.363
This is terrible.

17:55.397 --> 17:57.365
Those robots are not
your friends.

17:57.399 --> 18:00.034
Yeah, well, at least they
don't steal from me.

18:00.068 --> 18:03.037
Look, I'm really sorry
I stole your jokes.

18:03.071 --> 18:04.705
It was a rotten
thing to do.

18:04.740 --> 18:06.374
You may not want me
back as a friend,

18:06.408 --> 18:08.376
but you deserve better
than those robots.

18:08.410 --> 18:11.045
Of course I want
you back, Brian.

18:11.079 --> 18:13.714
The fact is-- I miss
hanging out with you.

18:13.749 --> 18:15.716
I'll tell you what,
let's hang out tonight

18:15.751 --> 18:18.386
after they see how many slaps
it takes to give me a stutter.

18:18.420 --> 18:20.054
Utewie, you got to put
a stop to this.

18:20.088 --> 18:22.056
I mean, you made them--
you can destroy them.

18:22.090 --> 18:25.192
What do you say you and I,
we take these robots out?

18:25.227 --> 18:27.828
You'd... you'd help me do that?

18:27.863 --> 18:29.997
Of course, Stewie,
I'm your friend.

18:30.032 --> 18:31.999
All right,
let's do it.

18:32.034 --> 18:33.668
Thank you, Brian.

18:33.702 --> 18:35.002
Okay, let's wrap it up.

18:35.037 --> 18:36.671
I reserved this time

18:36.705 --> 18:39.006
to listen to Metallica
and flex in the mirror.

18:39.041 --> 18:41.175
He's right; it's
on the whiteboard.

18:44.713 --> 18:47.348
Peter, what is that?

18:47.382 --> 18:50.017
This, Lois, is
our old mattress.

18:50.052 --> 18:51.352
Well, get it out of here.

18:51.386 --> 18:54.021
It smells like
John Popper's cargo shorts.

18:54.056 --> 18:56.524
No, it smells
like our marriage.

18:56.558 --> 18:57.525
What?!

18:57.559 --> 18:58.859
Don't you see, Lois?

18:58.894 --> 19:00.861
This mattress is
a living tapestry

19:00.896 --> 19:02.196
of everything we've
done together.

19:02.230 --> 19:03.864
Every stain, a story.

19:03.899 --> 19:06.233
Every smudge, a chapter
in our family's life.

19:06.268 --> 19:08.569
This mark here is from
where we conceived Meg.

19:08.603 --> 19:09.904
Over here was Chris.

19:09.938 --> 19:11.572
And all the way up
here was Stewie,

19:11.606 --> 19:13.941
'cause, remember, you coughed
up all that pool water?

19:13.975 --> 19:17.044
Oh, Peter,
you were so handsome.

19:17.079 --> 19:20.715
Lois, this mattress may be old
and worn-in, but so are we.

19:20.749 --> 19:24.051
And I wouldn't trade
you in for anything.

19:28.090 --> 19:29.724
You know, I, uh, think

19:29.758 --> 19:32.393
I still got a stain
or two left inside me.

19:32.427 --> 19:34.428
Oh, Peter.

19:36.431 --> 19:39.066
Yeah, I want to do you
right where the porn lunch was.

19:39.101 --> 19:40.735
What?

19:40.769 --> 19:43.070
I said, I want to do you
right where the porn lunch was.

19:43.105 --> 19:44.972
God, I wish you'd listen.

19:50.746 --> 19:53.380
Stewie, three more
Arnold Palmers.

19:53.415 --> 19:55.716
Boy, we're destroying them
at the right time, Brian.

19:55.751 --> 19:58.052
I don't have enough iced
tea for the correct ratio.

19:58.086 --> 19:59.053
It'll be too lemonade-y.

19:59.087 --> 20:00.054
They'll be furious.

20:00.088 --> 20:01.388
All right,
so let's do it.

20:01.423 --> 20:02.757
Let's take 'em out.

20:02.791 --> 20:04.425
I'll warn you,
it's not gonna be easy.

20:04.459 --> 20:05.760
They're incredibly intelligent

20:05.794 --> 20:07.094
and getting smarter
by the minute.

20:07.129 --> 20:09.096
I designed them to be
constantly adapting...

20:09.131 --> 20:10.765
It's done, I sprayed 'em
with the hose.

20:18.473 --> 20:20.441
Ah, boy, that was
the best night's sleep

20:20.475 --> 20:22.109
I've had
in a long time, Lois.

20:22.144 --> 20:23.778
Same with me.

20:23.812 --> 20:25.780
You know, I'm glad we're
keeping our old mattress.

20:25.814 --> 20:27.782
Sometimes newer
isn't better.

20:27.816 --> 20:29.784
Yeah.

20:29.818 --> 20:31.452
Are your privates itchy, too,
or just mine?

20:31.486 --> 20:32.787
No, they're itchy.

20:32.821 --> 20:34.121
Maybe we should keep
the new mattress.

20:34.156 --> 20:35.456
Way ahead of you, Lois.

20:35.490 --> 20:37.124
I already dragged
the old one out to the curb.

20:37.159 --> 20:40.161
Good. Okay, I'm gonna go rub up
against the basement doorjamb.

20:41.530 --> 20:43.497
Stewie, I really am sorry
about what happened.

20:43.532 --> 20:44.832
Oh, don't mention it.

20:44.866 --> 20:46.834
I'm just glad to have
the whole mess behind us.

20:46.868 --> 20:49.003
So what'd you end up doing
with those old robots anyway?

20:49.037 --> 20:51.005
I just left them out
on the curb for the trash man.

20:51.006 --> 20:55.406
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru

20:55.409 --> 20:57.410
How can this
not be a trap?